WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.900
Sanelle: private, practical support for living with fibroids.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.900
First: understanding her diagnosis.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.395
Meet Thandi. Today shows one helpful next step.

00:00:11.545 --> 00:00:15.114
She adds the report she was given.

00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:18.007
A fictional demo report, for this video.

00:00:18.157 --> 00:00:23.379
The phone reads it on the device. Nothing is uploaded.

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:28.751
She compares each measurement with the original wording.

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.470
Only the details she checked are saved.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:38.668
What the report doesn’t say stays unknown, never guessed.

00:00:38.818 --> 00:00:44.453
A missing detail becomes a question for her doctor.

00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:48.172
Next, a quick daily check-in.

00:00:48.322 --> 00:00:52.305
She picks what showed up today.

00:00:52.455 --> 00:00:58.090
Bleeding in her own words, not invented millilitres.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.222
And how it affected her day.

00:01:02.372 --> 00:01:07.181
Her history counts only recorded days, and shows the gaps.

00:01:07.331 --> 00:01:15.445
Appointment brings it together: her report, her symptoms and her questions.

00:01:15.595 --> 00:01:19.164
She sets her main concern.

00:01:19.314 --> 00:01:27.429
The question from her report is ready for the visit.

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:33.627
Afterwards, she records the answer and the agreed next step.

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:42.288
Back on Today, that next step is waiting.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.420
Second: Sanelle AI, live.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:50.841
First, suggestions from patterns in her own check-ins.

00:01:50.991 --> 00:01:58.907
Sanelle AI asks first: what’s read, who processes it, and that she checks every word.

00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:03.085
Real AI questions, from her two check-ins.

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:10.915
Each shows why, with the real counts behind it. Nothing invented.

00:02:11.065 --> 00:02:15.535
She rewrites it in her own words.

00:02:15.685 --> 00:02:19.279
Only what she adds is saved.

00:02:19.429 --> 00:02:25.155
Her exact words, matched to a published research explanation.

00:02:25.305 --> 00:02:30.147
With its limits and sources.

00:02:32.528 --> 00:02:37.407
Her chosen question is ready for the visit.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:43.647
Now Sanelle AI drafts her main concern.

00:02:43.797 --> 00:02:55.829
A first-person draft from her real counts and her own words. Labelled as AI, and not a medical summary.

00:02:55.979 --> 00:03:13.684
She edits every word before saving. Every draft is checked first: unsupported numbers, diagnoses, causes and quotes she never wrote are removed.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:17.816
Her edited concern is saved.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:32.840
Safety in three points: drafts are checked; if nothing passes, her own words stay; and nothing is saved unless she chooses Add or Save.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.940
Third: food, without the fear.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:40.022
Practical food support. No banned lists.

00:03:40.172 --> 00:03:44.154
She reviews her food requirements.

00:03:44.304 --> 00:03:49.526
A vegetarian pattern, plus anything she avoids.

00:03:49.676 --> 00:03:54.485
And what makes cooking easier for her.

00:03:54.635 --> 00:04:01.097
Sanelle previews a week of meals that fit.

00:04:01.247 --> 00:04:04.816
The plan is saved.

00:04:04.966 --> 00:04:09.361
She follows the recipe, step by step.

00:04:09.511 --> 00:04:14.733
And taps “I made this” when it’s done.

00:04:14.883 --> 00:04:27.725
The shopping list comes from her plan. She ticks what she already has.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.860
Finally: what the research says.

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:41.355
Plain-language research summaries, grouped by topic.

00:04:41.505 --> 00:04:47.223
Each gives a short answer, and where the evidence falls short.

00:04:47.373 --> 00:04:52.636
Who was studied, the sources, and the limits.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.780
Sanelle. Her records, her words, her decisions.
